    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **263 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI made the `householdId` deterministic and rewired household duplicate detection in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`.\n\n**Behavior changes implemented:**\n\n1. **Deterministic householdId** \u2014 Now computed as the first 12 upper-case hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`, where `normalizedLastName` is the trimmed/whitespace-collapsed/lower-cased last name. It's assigned to every owner that has a postcode; an owner with no postcode has no household (`householdId` stays null, so `identityKey` keeps its `+tel||` form).\n\n2. **Household duplicate = same (lastName, postcode)** \u2014 Before persisting, the code checks whether any existing owner resolves to the same computed householdId. If so, the create is rejected with **409** unless the request sets `sharesHousehold`, in which case the owner is created as a declared household member.\n\n3. **`sharesHousehold` only bypasses the block** \u2014 It no longer creates/propagates the link (the link is now automatic via the deterministic id); it just skips the 409. A declared member is explicitly **not** flagged as a possible duplicate (`possibleDuplicate=false`), rather than running the soft-match that would otherwise flag it since it shares last name + postcode.\n\n4. **Duplicate detection keys off the computed householdId** \u2014 the `identityKey` check uses the deterministic value on both the new and existing owners.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 replaced the old (lastName, address) household-matching block; added `computeHouseholdId(Owner)`; updated `householdId(...)` to take the postcode; removed the now-unused `ArrayList` import.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 updated the `householdId` and `sharesHousehold` field descriptions to match the new semantics.\n\nThe `membershipLevel` had no household-size input in this codebase (it's email + namesake-based, per the spec's \"level 4 reserved for tenure\"), so no change was needed there.",
